  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/LostBeard/SpawnDev.Reachy",
  "published": "2026-09-16T17:07:46.907Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.1.0-preview.3 - FIXES ReachyEars, which in preview.2 delivered no audio at all. The robot's remote audio track reports live and unmuted (the browser only unmutes once RTP is arriving), and a MediaStreamTrackProcessor built on it still sat on a read that never completed and never threw: Chrome does not run the decode pipeline for a remote audio track that nothing renders. ReachyEars now attaches its own muted, off-screen audio element as that sink - muted so the robot's microphone is not played into the room it is listening to, and so it stays inside the autoplay policy on a page with no user gesture. VERIFIED on hardware: 480-sample frames at 48 kHz, 803 chunks with live room levels. Also reports the track's readyState, muted and enabled the moment media arrives, and logs mute/unmute/ended transitions - a present-but-silent track is otherwise indistinguishable from a broken capture.",
